    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense centers today around **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 78.15 efficiency score makes him the premier start of the afternoon. Facing Kremer, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 14% platoon adjustment and the stability of the leadoff spot, providing the safest floor for R/RBI production. **Jacob Wilson** (65.32) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.95) represent our next tier of high-conviction plays; **Jacob Wilson** is particularly well-positioned given the 10% park factor boost in his matchup against Peralta, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** maintains a strong profile despite a challenging individual matchup against Gray. **Andy Pages** (60.44) also clears our 60-point start threshold, as his prime placement in the two-hole against Cameron allows him to capitalize on the favorable platoon environment.\n\nConversely, our lower-end starts show the volatility of the back-half of the order. **Jackson Merrill** (50.37) draws a tough assignment against Henderson (2.82 xERA), which severely hampers his ceiling, and **Coby Mayo** (43.96) and **Luis Lara** (40.41) are teetering near the bench threshold. **Wade Meckler** serves as the most notable exclusion; his 35.04 score fell short of our 40.0 floor due to a disadvantageous L/L matchup against Gore and a weak #9 spot in the lineup. While **Drake Baldwin** earns a spot at 54.36, his start is driven primarily by his lead-off assignment, as his raw matchup against Scott remains middling. We will continue to monitor **Jordan Westburg**\u2019s status on the IL, as his absence\u2014along with the rest days for **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**\u2014continues to squeeze our depth in this 5x5 Roto grind. No acute weather threats are currently forecasted, but the high xERA of our opponent starters suggests a day where we should remain aggressive in chasing run environments, provided we respect the game-cap limits for our secondary options.",
